            <div xml:id="d525">

                <pb facs="0644" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. John C. Wright to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 14.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 18, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi> :* * * * * </p>
                <p>Count Bismarck, in presenting the draft of the constitution to the federal
                    Parliament, made a few remarks. I herewith enclose you the same in English.
                    Several hostile speeches have been delivered against the present draft, and
                    Count Bismarck has replied to such attacks in most vigorous language. (See
                    enclosed speeches.) The opposition comes mostly from the Catholic party, and the
                    delegates from Saxony and Hanover.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN C. WRIGHT.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D, C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d525-a1.xml" xpointer="d525-a1"/>
